---
import site from '../data/site.json';

const glam2Label = `$${site.glam2_cost_usd.toFixed(2)}`;
const costLabel = `$${site.cost_usd.toFixed(2)}`;
const millipore = site.millipore_cost_usd.toLocaleString('en-US');
---
<section id="why">
  <div class="eyebrow">Why</div>
  <h2>The measurement is solved. Producing the instrument isn't.</h2>
  <p class="lead">
    <em>E. coli</em> membrane filtration is the measurement WHO and UNICEF
    use in household drinking-water quality surveys. The instrument that
    performs it is not the open problem.
  </p>

  <div class="stat-row">
    <div class="stat">
      <div class="num">{site.context.population_without_safe_water_bn} bn</div>
      <div class="label">people without safely managed drinking water</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stat">
      <div class="num">{site.context.population_without_water_quality_data_pct}%</div>
      <div class="label">of the global population lacks any water-quality data at all</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>
    Testing this many sites needs many instruments, not one better one. The
    steel Millipore EZ-Fit™ manifold — the reference instrument this device
    is validated against — retails around <strong>${millipore.toString()}</strong>,
    is centrally manufactured, and is a closed design: it cannot be produced
    locally, only bought.
  </p>
  <p>
    UNICEF's own second-generation lightweight affordable manifold
    (<strong>2GLAM</strong>) already solved the cost problem, bringing the
    per-unit price to about {glam2Label}. What it does not solve is
    <strong>availability</strong> — it too is centrally produced from a
    proprietary design. 3DPLAM's contribution is not a cheaper manifold
    (at about {costLabel} it happens to also be cheaper); it is an
    <strong>open, locally 3D-printable</strong> one — a design anyone with
    an FDM printer can produce, repair and modify themselves, without
    waiting on a supply chain.
  </p>
</section>

<style>
  #why h2 { max-width: 20ch; margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .stat-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 20px;
    margin: 32px 0 36px;
  }
  .stat {
    padding: 22px 24px;
    background: var(--bg-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }
  .stat .num {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 40px;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .stat .label {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--fg-dim);
    line-height: 1.45;
    max-width: none;
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .stat-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
